    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81237.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "So obviously here at the American Conservation Coalition's conference, there's a lot of talk about conservative solutions to the issue of climate change. I wanted to sort of get your sense on how Republicans approach this issue, how you think they should approach the issue, and particularly for Republican voters who care about the environment may believe that certain things need to be done, but so much of what proliferates In Washington and in the news media about what these solutions are supposed to be, they don't fit, you know, conservatives tend to not necessarily agree with all of that. So how do you approach all of this?",
