    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "So I think everybody is intellectually honest and the colleagues I serve with Republicans know that human activity has an impact where you get called the climate deniers, where you start questioning what is that impact? If you want to understand how much is the impact and how much should we invest and work on solutions to mitigate that impact, that's where you get the differences. And the left is that I think they wake up every morning scared to death and alarmed that if we don't set our hair on fire today about the climate, then you're a climate denier. So I'd like to say that the left has a climate agenda. Republicans and conservatives have a climate plan. We have an energy plan. If you look at what's happening under Joe Biden's leadership, under Democrats and Congress' leadership, it's a total failure. Their energy policy is terrible. They're causing more greenhouse gas emissions with their energy policy than we've had before. The demand for energy hasn't gone away and guess what? It's not going to go away. So if we're not producing it here in the U.S. in the cleanest, safest, most efficient way possible, you see Joe Biden going to Saudi Arabia, same asking Venezuela and Iran for more oil. We're putting it on a boat and chipping it across the ocean, emitting a lot of carbon versus taking it out of Canada and putting it into pop line that was going to use all renewable energy to transport that oil to the refineries in the Gulf. Natural gas has allowed the US to reduce greenhouse gas emissions more than any other country in the world, more than anybody in the Paris Climate Accords combined, yet they're demonizing natural gas. Maybe someday we can get rid of natural gas, but it's not tomorrow.",
